---

### Answers to Review Questions

1. **Are the judgments a faithful statement of the decided surface rules, and do they encode any rule or spelling that is NOT decided?**
   - **UTF-8 and ASCII identifier rules**: `Utf8.Decodes` and `IdentStart`/`IdentContinue` match `SYN-5@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1076-1078](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1076-L1078)) and `SYN-6@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1078-1079](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1078-L1079)).
   - **Undecided rules encoded**:
     - `SourceOk` ([ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:57-58](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L57-L58)) encodes a pre-lexing refusal `∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF` across the entire decoded scalar stream, and `DecodeReason` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:18-26](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L18-L26)) / `checkSource` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:183-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L183-L187)) refuse `.nul` and `.bom` at any offset in the file (even inside comments or future string literals, and conflating a leading byte-order mark at offset 0 with `U+FEFF` at offset `> 0`, as in [Concrete/Lex.lean:427](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L427)). Neither `SYN-5@3` nor any owner decision in `docs/decisions.md` decides a source-wide `U+0000`/`U+FEFF` pre-filter.
     - `LineComment` ([ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:70-82](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L70-L82)) treats bare `CR` (`13`, `\r` without `\n`) as terminating a `//` line comment (`LineEnd c := c = 10 ∨ c = 13`). This is not in `docs/decisions.md`, departs from the reference lexer ([legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean:90-95](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean#L90-L95) and [legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md:11](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/docs/spec/syntax.md#L11), which end `//` comments only at `\n` or EOF), and introduces the classic lone-`CR` comment-termination hazard (`// ...\r<code on same line in LF-only editors>`).
2. **Are the theorems the right ones (soundness, completeness, determinism), non-vacuous, and at the right layer for the long term (spec vs implementation)?**
   - **Layering is wrong**: Pure specification theorems (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `lineComment_unique`) live in [Concrete/Lex.lean:105-180](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L105-L180) and [Concrete/Lex.lean:377-382](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L377-L382) instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean` (see [Concrete/README.md:161](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L161) and `ROADMAP.md` R-0560). Furthermore, `ConcreteSpec` already has a UTF-8 specification in [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean:513-539](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean#L513-L539) (`ConcreteSpec.Borrow.Utf8`), creating a duplicate normative definition.
   - **Missing error-soundness / first-error-offset theorem**: `decode_sound`/`decode_complete` only characterize `.ok cs`. There is no theorem that `.error e` reports a real error at the first invalid byte offset; [changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md#L5-L6) defers the first-error-offset theorem as a TODO.
   - **Redundant hypothesis**: `checkSource_complete` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:319-320](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L319-L320)) takes both `(hd : Utf8.Decodes bs cs)` and `(hs : SourceOk bs)`, where `SourceOk bs` already existentially packages `Utf8.Decodes bs cs`.
3. **Is the decoder correct on edge cases (overlongs, surrogates, `> U+10FFFF`, truncation, error offsets)?**
   - On valid vs. invalid byte sequences (`.ok` vs `.error`), `Utf8.One`/`Two`/`Three`/`Four` and `decode` accurately enforce Unicode Table 3-7 (rejecting `0xC0..0xC1`, `0xE0 0x80..0x9F`, `0xF0 0x80..0x8F` overlongs; `0xED 0xA0..0xBF` surrogates; `0xF4 0x90..0xBF` and `0xF5..0xFF` out-of-range; `0x80..0xBF` lone continuations; and truncated sequences).
   - On error offsets and execution behavior, `decodeAt`, `sourceAt`, and `badSequence` have structural flaws:
     - `sourcePrepend off a.toNat (sourceAt (off + 1) bs)` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:183-210](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L183-L210)) claims to *"Refuse NUL or BOM before inspecting the remaining source"*, but in Lean's call-by-value semantics, the recursive argument `sourceAt (off + 1) bs` is evaluated to the end of the input *before* `sourcePrepend` runs.
     - Both `decodeAt` and `sourceAt` recurse in non-tail position and inspect up to 4 bytes even when the lead byte `a` has already determined a 1-, 2-, or 3-byte sequence.
     - `badSequence` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:43](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L43)) reports `.unexpectedContinuation` when a multi-byte lead is followed by a *non*-continuation ASCII byte (`b < 0x80`, e.g. `[0xC2, 0x41]` in [Concrete/Lex.lean:412](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L412)).
4. **Is the axiom golden consistent (`propext` or none)?**
   - The 15 generated entries in [scripts/proofs/axioms.golden:549-563](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/scripts/proofs/axioms.golden#L549-L563) (injectivity/sizeOf lemmas for `LineComment` and matcher equations for `instDecidableLineComment`, using at most `propext`) are consistent with the rest of `axioms.golden`. However, user-written theorems are absent from `axioms.golden` only because they were put in `Concrete/Lex.lean` instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean`.
5. **Anything that would let a wrong lexer pass the gates?**
   - **Yes**: `scripts/proofs/*` checks only `ConcreteSpec`, and `scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` checks only the theorem list in [Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72). None of `Concrete.Lex`'s theorems were added to `Concrete.Premises.theorems`, and `trust_ban.sh` does not scan `Concrete/`. A `sorry`, `native_decide`, extra axiom, or banned `set_option` in `Concrete/Lex.lean` passes every gate today—and in fact [Concrete/Lex.lean:13](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L13) and [Concrete/Lex.lean:402](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L402) already use `set_option maxRecDepth`, which `trust_ban.sh` forbids.

