### Findings

#### 1. [HIGH] Undecided lexical rules encoded in `Surface0` and `Concrete.Lex` (source-wide NUL/BOM pre-refusal and bare-`CR` line-comment termination)
- **Locations**:
  - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:4-5](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L4-L5), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:56-59](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L56-L59), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:70-82](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L70-L82), [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:122-123](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L122-L123)
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:18-26](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L18-L26), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187), [Concrete/Lex.lean:345-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L345-L351), [Concrete/Lex.lean:424-429](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L424-L429), [Concrete/Lex.lean:435](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L435)
- **Problem**:
  1. `SourceOk` (`∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`) encodes a source-wide ban on `U+0000` and `U+FEFF` at every position in the file prior to lexing, and classifies any `U+FEFF` anywhere in the file (even at byte offset `> 0`, e.g. [Concrete/Lex.lean:427](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L427)) as `.bom`. `SYN-5@3` ([docs/decisions.md:1076-1078](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/docs/decisions.md#L1076-L1078)) states only that *"A source file is UTF-8 text"*; no owner decision establishes a pre-lexing `U+0000`/`U+FEFF` filter over the whole file (which would also ban `U+FEFF` inside comments and string literals).
  2. `LineEnd c := c = 10 ∨ c = 13` makes bare `CR` (`13`) end a `//` line comment. Neither `SYN-6@3` nor any owner decision approves bare `CR` as a line terminator; the frozen compiler ended `//` comments only at `LF` (`10`) or EOF ([legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean:90-95](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/legacy/Concrete/Frontend/Lexer.lean#L90-L95)). Allowing bare `CR` to terminate a `//` comment lets code hidden after `\r` on the same `\n`-delimited line execute.
- **Long-term fix**:
  Remove undecided character/line-ending rules from `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and `Concrete/Lex.lean`. If a specific policy on leading UTF-8 BOM, control characters (`NUL`, bare `CR`), and line endings is desired for `Surface0`, present the options and a recommendation (e.g., `LF` / `CRLF` line endings only, refusing bare `CR` outside string escapes, and handling non-token characters in the token grammar) to the owner first and record the owner's dated answer in `docs/decisions.md` before encoding it in `ConcreteSpec`.

#### 2. [HIGH] Duplicate UTF-8 specification in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` and specification theorems placed in the compiler (`Concrete/Lex.lean`) instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/`
- **Locations**:
  - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:11-53](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L11-L53) vs. [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean:513-539](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean#L513-L539)
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:105-120](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L105-L120) (`encodes_scalar`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:168-180](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L168-L180) (`decodes_unique`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:377-382](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L377-L382) (`lineComment_unique`)
  - [ConcreteSpec.lean:1-7](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec.lean#L1-L7)
- **Problem**:
  1. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Borrow.lean` already defines UTF-8 scalar well-formedness (`ConcreteSpec.Borrow.isScalar`, `ConcreteSpec.Borrow.Utf8`), with `utf8_split` and `text_view_utf8` proved in `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Borrow.lean`. `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` introduces a second, unconnected UTF-8 definition (`ConcreteSpec.Surface0.Utf8`), violating P2 ("one authoritative definition") and R-0560/R-0571.
  2. Pure specification theorems about `ConcreteSpec.Surface0` (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `encodes_step_unique`, `encodes_determ`, `lineComment_unique`) are placed in `Concrete/Lex.lean` instead of `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean` (cf. [Concrete/README.md:161](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L161)). As a result, `scripts/spec/lean_site.sh` displays `0` theorems for `Surface0` in the owner view, and none of the four proof-integrity gates (`axioms.sh`, `trust_ban.sh`, `kernel_replay.sh`, `external.sh`) check these theorems.
- **Long-term fix**:
  Unify the UTF-8 definition in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` so source decoding and `Text`/`Borrow` share one authoritative UTF-8 specification, move the specification-level theorems (`encodes_scalar`, `decodes_unique`, `lineComment_unique`, and their helper lemmas) into `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Surface0.lean`, and import `ConcreteSpec.Proofs.Surface0` in `ConcreteSpec.lean` (updating `scripts/proofs/axioms.golden` accordingly).

#### 3. [HIGH] Unproved error reporting, non-short-circuiting non-tail recursion in `decodeAt`/`sourceAt`, and deferred first-error-offset TODO
- **Locations**:
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:31-51](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L31-L51) (`badSequence`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:58-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L58-L80) (`decodeAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:182-212](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L212) (`sourcePrepend`, `sourceAt`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351) (`scanLine`)
  - [changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md#L5-L6)
- **Problem**:
  1. `sourcePrepend` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:182-187](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L182-L187)) states `/-- Refuse NUL or BOM before inspecting the remaining source. -/`, and is called as `sourcePrepend off a.toNat (sourceAt (off + 1) bs)`. Because Lean 4 is call-by-value, `sourceAt (off + 1) bs` is evaluated across the entire remainder of the file *before* `sourcePrepend` executes.
  2. Both `decodeAt` and `sourceAt` duplicate the 4-way match, recurse in non-tail position (`prepend ... (decodeAt ...)`), and inspect up to 4 bytes `[a, b, c, d]` before calling `badSequence` even when `a` is a 1-, 2-, or 3-byte lead that already failed at `a` or `b`. Similarly, `scanLine` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:348-351](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L348-L351)) is non-tail-recursive.
  3. `badSequence` ([Concrete/Lex.lean:43](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L43)) labels a non-continuation byte (`b < 0x80 ∨ b > 0xBF`, such as ASCII `0x41` after `0xC2` in [Concrete/Lex.lean:412](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L412)) as `.unexpectedContinuation` even when `b` is not a continuation byte.
  4. No theorem connects `.error e` to the specification; the first-error-offset theorem was deferred as a TODO in `changelog.d/2026-11-08-lexer-utf8.md:5-6`. Under the 2026-11-08 owner rule (never cut corners; implement the best long-term design), shipping an unproved `badSequence` sidecar and deferring the error theorem is a shortcut.
- **Long-term fix**:
  Factor single-scalar decoding into one total step function `decodeStep (off : Nat) (bs : List UInt8) : Except DecodeError (Nat × Nat × List UInt8)` that dispatches on the lead byte's length class and fails immediately at the first offending byte, iterate it tail-recursively so execution short-circuits on the first error in $O(1)$ stack space, distinguish a missing continuation byte from a lone continuation byte, and prove the first-error-offset soundness theorem now rather than leaving a TODO.

#### 4. [HIGH] `Concrete/Lex.lean` is completely outside the proof-integrity and trusted-base gates, and relies on `set_option maxRecDepth`
- **Locations**:
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:13](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L13) (`set_option maxRecDepth 2048`), [Concrete/Lex.lean:402](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L402) (`set_option maxRecDepth 100000`)
  - [Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)
  - [tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt:10-16](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt#L10-L16)
  - [scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:42-50](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L42-L50)
- **Problem**:
  1. `scripts/proofs/*` checks only `ConcreteSpec`, and `scripts/checks/compiler/slice0_trusted_base.sh` checks only the theorem names listed in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` ([Concrete/Premises.lean:64-72](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Premises.lean#L64-L72)). Because `Concrete.Lex`'s theorems are not registered in `Concrete.Premises.theorems` and `trust_ban.sh` does not scan `Concrete/`, a `sorry`, `native_decide`, or extra axiom in `Concrete/Lex.lean` would pass every gate.
  2. `Concrete/Lex.lean` already uses `set_option maxRecDepth 2048` (line 13) and `set_option maxRecDepth 100000` (line 402), which `scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh:46` bans (`\bset_option\b`) and [Concrete/README.md:505](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L505) (Gate 2) bans across `Concrete/`. Needing `maxRecDepth 100000` to run `by decide` on 9-byte examples also shows that the `Decidable` instances in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:88-110` will blow the kernel reducer stack on real slice-0 certificate checks (`cert_denotes ... := by decide`, [Concrete/README.md:451-452](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L451-L452)).
- **Long-term fix**:
  Extend `trust_ban.sh` (or `slice0_trusted_base.sh`) to enforce the trust ban over `Concrete/`, register `Concrete.Lex`'s soundness and completeness theorems in `Concrete/Premises.lean` and `tests/golden/slice0_trusted_base.txt`, and eliminate both `set_option maxRecDepth` directives by proving `Decidable` through boolean reflection (`iff` to a tail-recursive boolean checker) rather than deep dependent `dite` chains.

#### 5. [MEDIUM] Redundant hypothesis in `checkSource_complete`, missing iff/negative-completeness forms, and unnecessary list allocation in `LineComment`
- **Locations**:
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:319-330](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L319-L330) (`checkSource_complete`)
  - [Concrete/Lex.lean:384-398](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/Lex.lean#L384-L398) (`lineComment_sound`, `lineComment_complete`)
  - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:78-80](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L78-L80) (`LineComment`)
- **Problem**:
  1. `checkSource_complete` requires both `(hd : Utf8.Decodes bs cs)` and `(hs : SourceOk bs)`, even though `SourceOk bs` is `∃ cs, Utf8.Decodes bs cs ∧ ∀ c ∈ cs, c ≠ 0 ∧ c ≠ 0xFEFF`.
  2. Neither `decode` nor `lineComment` exposes the packaged bidirectional equivalence (`decode bs = .ok cs ↔ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`, `lineComment cs = some out ↔ LineComment cs out`) or the negative soundness lemma (`decode bs = .error e → ∀ cs, ¬ Utf8.Decodes bs cs`).
  3. `LineComment` constructs `47 :: 47 :: body` even though comments are trivia discarded by the lexer ([Concrete/README.md:214](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/Concrete/README.md#L214)), forcing `scanLine` to allocate a copy of every comment character.
- **Long-term fix**:
  State and prove the clean bidirectional `↔` theorems (`decode_ok_iff`, `lineComment_some_iff`) and error-refusal lemmas (`decode_error_not_decodes`), and model comment skipping in `Surface0` as consuming comment trivia to the remaining suffix `rest` (or span length) without allocating a discarded `47 :: 47 :: body` list.

#### 6. [LOW] `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits the `PROPOSED` module-header convention and decision-row citations
- **Locations**:
  - [ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean:1-8](file:///tmp/claude-30035/-home-unbalancedparen-projects-concrete2/e2c54e65-31b5-4145-8101-c2d7b071b97e/scratchpad/rev-lexw1a/src/ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean#L1-L8)
- **Problem**:
  Every other module in `ConcreteSpec/Spec/` carries the `PROPOSED: not normative until the owner freezes Core (ROADMAP A2c). Part of ConcreteSpec.Spec; see ConcreteSpec/README.md.` header, and `ROADMAP.md:331` / `docs/proposals/SPEC_UNIFICATION.md:758-759` require each spec rule's doc comment to cite the `docs/decisions.md` row it encodes (`SYN-5@3`, `SYN-6@3`). `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` omits both.
- **Long-term fix**:
  Add the standard `PROPOSED` header to `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Surface0.lean` and cite the governing decision rows in each declaration's doc comment.

